 come from this summit but  the two leaders welcomed the opportunity  for frank conversations  for more i'm joined by dw correspondent  uh washington correspondent oliver salad  and beijing based journalist fabian  kreshma oliver let's start with you  biden initiated this virtual meeting to  help defuse tensions now did he get what  he was hoping for  well tell me he did certainly not go  into these consultations with big  expectations with regards to the outcome  so what he wanted to do here is to  revive some good old diplomacy if you  will knowing that this is probably the  best way to avoid confrontation of the  two countries  actually this virtual summit this  virtual meeting was considered the first  formal meeting between the two  presidents if you take out some phone  calls that were made  throughout the year they have never met  in person since president biden took  office and that's almost one year ago so  we have the two biggest economies at the  table here  with military active in the same region  so certainly a long overdue conversation  fabian let's come to you now xi jinping  called for more communication and  cooperation uh between the two sides do  you see any scope for that  well if you listen closely then um xi  jinping even  called joe biden an old friend and of  course this is just symbolic  rhetoric but it is meaningful because we  come from really the worst bilateral  relations of the two countries in  more than three decades and um so it  shows really a genuine attempt that  china is hoping for a restart of  bilateral relations and xi jinping  singled out basically two fields for  cooperation and one is the global  climate change and the other one is  the  pandemic and those probably are the two  fields where there's the biggest overlap  of interest  between these two countries and probably  the only fields where we can see  immediate cooperation  uh these so-called old friends oliver uh  the u.s and china are at odds over many  issues which 